# tg.sh console, 2026-10-14 23:26:52 board time: does the host console (UART_TX pops) follow the
# generators? Each case is a 3-second `tanager-host --timeout 5 run` after `tg start`;
# UART_TX_LEVEL (0x104) is the number of bytes waiting for the host when run starts.
== A: tg start, 2 s, run 3 s
$ tanager-host tg start 16384
traffic generators running over 16384 lines each; window 0x840000000 + 0x40000000
$ tanager-host tg status
passes 119, lines checked 3887534, errors 0 (last at line 0x0000000)
$ tanager-host peek 0x104
0x00000116
run A: exit 124, 614 dots;  [tanager-host] timeout
== B: tg start, 2 s, injector 250 for 2 s, back to 0, run 3 s
$ tanager-host tg start 16384
traffic generators running over 16384 lines each; window 0x840000000 + 0x40000000
$ tanager-host --inj-rd 250 inj
$ tanager-host --inj-rd 0 inj
$ tanager-host tg status
passes 167, lines checked 5447063, errors 0 (last at line 0x0000000)
$ tanager-host peek 0x104
0x00000176
run B: exit 124, 710 dots;  [tanager-host] timeout
== C: tg start, run at once
$ tanager-host tg start 16384
traffic generators running over 16384 lines each; window 0x840000000 + 0x40000000
$ tanager-host peek 0x104
0x0000002a
run C: exit 124, 376 dots;  [tanager-host] timeout
